~ Combat
You try talking some sense to the guard..
- What is your origin?
	Guard: . . .
- Wait. We don't have to fight!
	Guard: I am sorry small one.
	Guard: I have given my all to lord . . .
	Guard: Nothing but my diligence remains.
- Please don't!
	The guards eyes seem to show some sympathy.
	Not enough to break his resolve..
- Prepare to die.
	You feel more courageous for saying that.
	The guard looks saddened by what he must do.
=> END

~ Overworld
if interacted == false:
	Blind Archer: Your voice trembles slightly
	Blind Archer: You are not where you belong are you little lamb
	Blind Archer: But I suppose this is the path fate guided for you
- Who are you?
	Blind Archer: Just a simple traveller
	=> Overworld
- Blind?
	Blind Archer: Yes, I removed my eyes myself
	Blind Archer: For in some ways you can see more without your sight
	Blind Archer: If you have any cloth on hand I could show you?
	- Hand over cloth 
		The blind man takes the cloth and fasions it into a simple blindfold
	- Leave
	=> Overworld
- Fight
	Blind Archer: If this is the end I was destined for so be it
	do relation.SetSeaRep(-10)
	set interacted = true
	set allowFight = true
	=> END
- Leave
=> END

~ FindItem
if item == null or amount <= 0
	You find nothing.
	=> END
else
	if amount == 1
		You find a [color=red]{{item.itemName}}[/color]!
	else
		You find [color=red]{{amount}} {{item.itemName}}s.[/color]
	do player.AddItem(item, amount)
set looted = true
=> END

~ LootBody
if looted == false
	You search the blind mans pockets.
	do GetLoot()
	=> FindItem
else
	The blind holds nothing.
=> END